Substitute "reach" by "solve" or "complete" then it's a valid rule even
for ascenders.

I usually see the game as to reach one little goal after the other, while
the sequence of goals is not fixed but rather depending on the evolution
of the specific game.  Then there are also sub-goals like finding bags,
reflection, magic resistance.  And finally there are problem specific
goals like remove all curses, identify all relevant loot, overcome that
bones level, etc.

BTW, Elloras story documents the application of such goals quite good,
though she is unspoiled and yet unaware of the major steps/goals you are
talking about, e.g. she don't know of Vlads Tower, etc.

Playing with plans and goals might be one key for solving the game.

